# The representative transform of a pair is chosen by the wrong components.
#
# align_patches.cpp groups the affine transforms sampled for a pair, takes their mean, and writes
# to rel.csv the sample nearest that mean. Its own comment says "how far the transformation part
# is from the mean", but the distance is measured in get<3> and get<5>. The affine is
# (a, b, tx, d, e, ty): get<2> and get<5> are the translation, get<3> is sin(-theta) and belongs
# to the rotation. So the sample was chosen by its rotation and its y translation, with the x
# translation taking no part.
#
# MEASURED, and it is what puts this patch in the inert group rather than in corrections.
# Box w035 of PHerc. 0139, seed 3455,2753,5383, 2858 seeds, stage g:
#   * instrumented run, both argmins computed side by side: 0 of 6,572 transformation groups
#     choose a different sample.
#   * isolation run, the reference tree plus this one line and nothing else: 1,495 of 1,495
#     patches identical byte for byte, rel.csv identical by sha256
#     (513860d84bdf6df13fb97c84732072fd8cf6e0ba7172a8d2c77aeb3db7a97777 both), surface.bp and
#     boundary.bp identical.
# The reason is not that the two distances agree: it is that within a group the accepted spread of
# the translation is small (MAX_TRANSLATE_VARIANCE, 2.2 quadmesh units at the limit) and the
# sample nearest the mean in one pair of coordinates happened to be the nearest in the other in
# every group of this run. On another field it need not be, which is why the line is repaired.
#
# Evidence: runs/rev1/audit/STEVENS-VALLE.md, runs/catena/superficie-stevens/out0139w035-rep.
--- a/pipeline9/align_patches.cpp
+++ b/pipeline9/align_patches.cpp
@@ -394,7 +394,10 @@
 				for(const affineTx &tx : tsIter.second)
 				{
 					// See how far the transformation part if from the mean
-					float distanceFromMean = pow(std::get<3>(tx)-std::get<3>(sampleMean),2) + pow(std::get<5>(tx)-std::get<5>(sampleMean),2);
+					// The translation of the affine is (get<2>, get<5>); get<3> is sin(-theta), part of the
+					// rotation. Measured in (sin theta, ty), the x translation took no part in the choice
+					// of the representative sample.
+					float distanceFromMean = pow(std::get<2>(tx)-std::get<2>(sampleMean),2) + pow(std::get<5>(tx)-std::get<5>(sampleMean),2);
 							
 					sampleVariance = affineTx(std::get<0>(sampleVariance)+pow(std::get<0>(tx)-std::get<0>(sampleMean),2),
 											  std::get<1>(sampleVariance)+pow(std::get<1>(tx)-std::get<1>(sampleMean),2),
